Bug 2077839 - Preserve encoded related-part data during size accounting. r=maxe, mkmelin

Hidden multipart/related leaves are decoded to calculate their attachment
size before their encoded content is buffered for compose replay. The
decoder overwrites its input, so Forward and Edit as New decode altered
data and create corrupt attachments even when replay and writes succeed.

Decode a scratch copy during size accounting to keep the original encoded
content intact while retaining accurate decoded attachment sizes.

Add xpcshell regression coverage that forwards orphan CID-bearing
attachments through the compose service and captures the complete SMTP
message. Compare each decoded attachment's name, exact size, and every
byte with its source. Cover memory and temporary-file buffering and both
base64 padding cases.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330742

diff --git a/mailnews/mime/src/mimeleaf.cpp b/mailnews/mime/src/mimeleaf.cpp
--- a/mailnews/mime/src/mimeleaf.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/mime/src/mimeleaf.cpp
@@ -7,8 +7,9 @@
 #include "nsMimeTypes.h"
 #include "prmem.h"
 #include "plstr.h"
 #include "prlog.h"
+#include "nsString.h"
 #include "nsMimeStringResources.h"
 #include "modmimee.h"  // for MimeConverterOutputCallback
 
 #define MIME_SUPERCLASS mimeObjectClass
@@ -192,9 +193,13 @@ int MimeLeaf_parse_buffer_for_size(const
                                    MimeObject* obj) {
   if (!obj || !mime_subclass_p(obj->clazz, (MimeObjectClass*)&mimeLeafClass))
     return 0;
 
-  return MimeLeaf_decode_buffer(buffer, size, obj, MimeLeaf_discard_decoded);
+  // Decoders overwrite their input. Preserve the encoded content, which
+  // multipart/related may buffer for later replay when composing.
+  nsAutoCStringN<128> bufferCopy(buffer, size);
+  return MimeLeaf_decode_buffer(bufferCopy.BeginWriting(), size, obj,
+                                MimeLeaf_discard_decoded);
 }
 
